---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout active="services" title="Services — Finding Forward">

  <section class="phead">
    <div class="wrap phead__wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Section — Services</p>
      <h1 class="display phead__h" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        Two ways of working,<br/>
        <em>chosen for fit,</em> not fashion.
      </h1>
      <p class="phead__lead" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
        Both approaches below are evidence-based and time-tested. In practice they
        overlap — we'll lean on whichever fits the texture of what you're carrying
        that week.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="dbt" class="srv srv--light">
    <div class="wrap srv__wrap">
      <aside class="srv__side" data-reveal>
        <span class="tag"><span class="pulse" style="background:var(--moss);"></span> Modality 01</span>
        <h2 class="display srv__h">Dialectical<br/>Behavior <em>Therapy.</em></h2>
        <p class="mono srv__meta">For: emotion regulation · relationships · self-harm urges · burnout</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="srv__body">
        <p class="srv__lead" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
          DBT was originally developed by Marsha Linehan for clients who felt
          consistently flooded — by feelings, by relationships, by the gap
          between intention and behavior. The framework has since spread
          because it works for a much wider audience: anyone who'd benefit from
          better tools for hard moments.
        </p>

        <div class="srv__cards">
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
            <p class="mono">Skill set 01</p>
            <h3>Mindfulness</h3>
            <p>Noticing what's actually happening — in the body, in the room, in the conversation — instead of the story we've spun about it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
            <p class="mono">Skill set 02</p>
            <h3>Distress tolerance</h3>
            <p>Riding waves you can't make go away. The micro-skills here keep painful moments from turning into damaging ones.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="4">
            <p class="mono">Skill set 03</p>
            <h3>Emotion regulation</h3>
            <p>Fewer 0-to-100 hijacks. We work on noticing earlier, naming better, and choosing what to do with the feeling.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="5">
            <p class="mono">Skill set 04</p>
            <h3>Interpersonal effectiveness</h3>
            <p>Asking, refusing, repairing. Practical scripts for the conversations we usually rehearse and then avoid.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://calendly.com/kevinrochelpc/consultation-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span>Try a DBT consult</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="self-compassion" class="srv srv--dark">
    <div class="wrap srv__wrap">
      <aside class="srv__side" data-reveal>
        <span class="tag"><span class="pulse" style="background:var(--clay);"></span> Modality 02</span>
        <h2 class="display srv__h">Self-Compassion<br/><em>Therapy.</em></h2>
        <p class="mono srv__meta">For: harsh inner critic · perfectionism · shame · burnout</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="srv__body">
        <p class="srv__lead" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
          Self-compassion is often misunderstood as letting yourself off the hook.
          It's not. It's the practice of speaking to yourself the way you'd speak
          to a friend in the same situation — and discovering that this gentler
          voice tends to produce more change, not less.
        </p>

        <div class="srv__cards">
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
            <p class="mono">Element 01</p>
            <h3>Self-kindness</h3>
            <p>Replacing reflexive self-criticism with the same warmth we extend, almost automatically, to others.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
            <p class="mono">Element 02</p>
            <h3>Common humanity</h3>
            <p>Naming the part of suffering that is universal. Struggle is not evidence of being uniquely broken.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="4">
            <p class="mono">Element 03</p>
            <h3>Mindful presence</h3>
            <p>Staying with what's painful without exaggerating it or pushing it away. The opposite of rumination.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="srv__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="5">
            <p class="mono">Element 04</p>
            <h3>Fierce compassion</h3>
            <p>Kindness with a backbone — the part that says no, sets limits, and protects the version of you trying to grow.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a class="btn btn-clay" href="https://calendly.com/kevinrochelpc/consultation-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span>Try a self-compassion consult</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="logistics">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The practical stuff</p>
      <h2 class="display logistics__h" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        Sessions, fees,<br/>and what to expect.
      </h2>
      <dl class="logistics__grid">
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
          <dt class="mono">Format</dt>
          <dd>Telehealth, secure video via Simple Practice. No app required — a link in your inbox is enough.</dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
          <dt class="mono">Length</dt>
          <dd>50 minutes, weekly. Twice-weekly available during stretches that call for it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
          <dt class="mono">Insurance</dt>
          <dd>Most major plans accepted in VA &amp; NY through Headway. We can check your benefits in a minute.</dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
          <dt class="mono">Private pay</dt>
          <dd>Sliding rates available. Invoiced monthly with receipts suitable for out-of-network reimbursement.</dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="4">
          <dt class="mono">Cancellation</dt>
          <dd>24-hour notice. We hold one another's time with care.</dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="4">
          <dt class="mono">Privacy</dt>
          <dd>HIPAA-compliant platform end to end. What's said here stays here.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .phead {
    padding: clamp(64px, 8vw, 120px) 0 clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px);
    background: var(--bone);
  }
  .phead__wrap { display: grid; gap: 22px; max-width: 1100px; }
  .phead__h { font-size: clamp(56px, 8vw, 128px); line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .phead__h em { color: var(--moss); }
  .phead__lead { font-size: 19px; max-width: 60ch; color: var(--ink-2); }

  .srv { padding: clamp(80px, 10vw, 140px) 0; }
  .srv--light { background: var(--bone-2); }
  .srv--dark { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
  .srv--dark .eyebrow, .srv--dark .mono { color: var(--sage); }
  .srv--dark .eyebrow::before { background: var(--sage); }
  .srv--dark .srv__lead { color: rgba(250,245,234,0.78); }
  .srv--dark .srv__card { background: var(--ink-2); border-color: rgba(250,245,234,0.12); }
  .srv--dark .srv__card h3 { color: var(--paper); }
  .srv--dark .srv__card p { color: rgba(250,245,234,0.78); }
  .srv--dark .srv__card .mono { color: var(--sun); }
  .srv--dark .srv__h em { color: var(--sun); }

  .srv__wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.45fr;
    gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .srv__side { display: grid; gap: 18px; position: sticky; top: 120px; align-content: start; }
  .srv__h {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 80px);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }
  .srv__h em {
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 100;
    color: var(--moss);
  }
  .srv__meta {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 16px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .srv--dark .srv__meta { border-color: rgba(250,245,234,0.14); }
  .srv__body { display: grid; gap: 32px; }
  .srv__lead { font-size: 19px; max-width: 60ch; color: var(--ink); }

  .srv__cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .srv__card {
    padding: 26px 24px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    align-content: start;
    transition: transform 0.5s var(--ease);
  }
  .srv__card:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); }
  .srv__card .mono { color: var(--clay); }
  .srv__card h3 { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .srv__card p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: none; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .srv__wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .srv__side { position: static; }
    .srv__cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .logistics {
    padding: clamp(80px, 10vw, 140px) 0;
    background: var(--bone);
  }
  .logistics__h {
    margin: 22px 0 clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.5vw, 80px);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .logistics__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .logistics__grid > div {
    background: var(--bone);
    padding: 28px 26px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .logistics__grid dt { color: var(--clay); }
  .logistics__grid dd { font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink); max-width: none; }

  @media (max-width: 880px) { .logistics__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
